imagine we are in a company that sell cloud hosting services.
we want to implement a class for storing data in cloud.
we have CloudStream that read or write data to the cloud.

manager said: hey "sometimes" we need encrypt data before storing on cloud!
              like when we store information about customer credit card.
              so we create EncryptCloudStream class for this

Note: we can't change write() method on CloudStream
      because we need storing plain data too!

manager said: hey "sometimes" we need compress data storing on cloud!
              like when data is huge and has low priority
              so we create "CompressedCloudStream" class for this

Note: we can't change write() method on CloudStream
      because we need storing plain data too!
      also we can't change write() method on EncryptCloudStream
      because we need store some encrypt data without compressing!


Problem: tomorrow manager said, hey "sometime" we need compress and encrypt data!
         we should implement it on another class like "EncryptCompressedCloudStream"
         but it's just duplicate code!
         if we have multiple functionalities the "Combination" of these functionalities
         (in combination the order is not the matter!
          in Permutation the order is matter!)
         is so countless, and we need separate class foe each one!
         it's not maintainable!
         we use Decorator Pattern to add additional behavior to an obj.
         so we can create just create base obj (like CloudStream obj)
         and add some functionalities that we want,
         "WE DECORATE BASE OBJECT WITH ADDITIONAL BEHAVIOR"
         like what we use to create some customise obj!